# Structures, alignments and predictions as the tools write them. Everything
# under data/ is either downloaded by a script in scripts/ or written by one,
# so none of it is tracked. data/README.md says what belongs there. On the
# machine this was developed on, data/ is not used at all: --data-dir points at
# the Linux filesystem and --cache-dir at the Windows one, for reasons given in
# data/README.md.
data/*
!data/README.md

# Model weights. AlphaFold2 parameters arrive as a tar of .npz files and Boltz-2
# as .ckpt files plus a tar of molecule definitions. Each set is gigabytes, is
# fetched into --cache-dir outside this tree, and is deleted before the next
# set is fetched. These rules exist so that a cache pointed at the wrong place
# cannot be staged.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.npz
*.tar
*.tar.gz
params/
weights/
.boltz/
colabfold_params/

# Structure downloads and raw prediction output. mmCIF and PDB files are
# re-fetchable from the accessions in config/ or regenerable from the tracked
# alignments, and there are thousands of them.
*.cif
*.cif.gz
*.pdb
*.pdb.gz
*.ent
*.ent.gz
*.bcif
*.mmtf
*.mmtf.gz
predictions/
colabfold_out/
boltz_results_*/

# The one exception to the rule above. Stage 3 of this roadmap has to choose
# between docking into the predicted PEDV spike and docking into 6U7K, and it
# needs the prediction itself to do that, so the handful of final PEDV models
# are tracked, compressed. Each is well under a megabyte.
!results/pedv/models/*.cif.gz

# Alignments. The uncompressed a3m files the MSA server returns are ignored;
# the gzipped copies in results/msa/ are tracked, because they are the only
# artefact that makes a prediction reproducible once the server's databases
# have moved on. The per-target confidence JSON (pLDDT and PAE) in
# results/confidence/ is tracked for the same reason and is not matched here.
*.a3m
*.m8

# Conda environment directories and package archives, if one is ever created
# inside the repository rather than under the conda root.
envs/
.conda/
conda-env/
.pixi/
*.conda
*.tar.bz2

# project.conf is written by scripts/00_configure.sh for one machine: thread
# count, memory ceiling, the measured sequence-length limit, absolute paths.
# Every clone regenerates its own.
project.conf
project.conf.tmp.*

# Per-stage logs. The timing and resource tables next to them are tracked,
# because the README quotes numbers out of them.
logs/*.log
logs/*.done
logs/tmp/

# Quarto and Jupyter build artefacts. The rendered report is kept.
*.html
!results/report/*.html
*_files/
.quarto/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
